\tag{fdip}
\title{Weights under inversion of all coordinates}
\date{2026-11-26}

\p{The inversion of \ref{fdip-013T} fixes one coordinate,
while the [spinor time map](fdip-017Z) reflects that coordinate.
What happens to the spin value when a charge conjugation
comes between the two maps? Which based link does an inverted
field see along a positive edge?}

\p{A determinant uses the entire grid. An observable may be
restricted to the links in one time half. How does total
inversion act on a weight of the first kind and on the domain
of the second?}

